@startuml epathmap-representation-states
' ============================================================================
' PathMap report §5.1 — the homogeneous EPathMap representation
'   EPathMap = Empty | Set(PathMap<()>) | Map(PathMap<Par>)
'
' Diagram type: a STATE DIAGRAM, chosen because the representation's defining
' property is a one-way MODE SELECTION: a neutral Empty commits to exactly one
' algebra (set or map) at the first membership operation, mixed membership is
' rejected, and a mode-dependent mutation on neutral Empty is refused with
' AmbiguousEmpty rather than guessed.  A state diagram is the only type that
' makes "which operations are answerable in which mode" legible at a glance.
'
' Colour convention — one hue per concept:
'   BLUE-GREY #ECEFF1/#455A64  the mode-neutral Empty
'   GREEN     #C8E6C9/#2E7D32  set mode — PathMap<()>
'   PURPLE    #E1BEE7/#6A1B9A  map mode — PathMap<Par>
'   AMBER     #FFE082/#EF6C00  the AmbiguousEmpty refusal
'   RED       #FFCDD2/#C62828  the mixed-membership rejection
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.4
skinparam ranksep 40
skinparam nodesep 30
skinparam StateBorderColor #455A64
skinparam StateBackgroundColor #ECEFF1

title <b>The homogeneous EPathMap representation</b>\none representation at a time: <latex>\mathtt{Empty}\;|\;\mathtt{Set}(\mathrm{PathMap}\langle()\rangle)\;|\;\mathtt{Map}(\mathrm{PathMap}\langle\mathrm{Par}\rangle)</latex>

state "**Empty**\nmode-neutral" as Empty #ECEFF1

state "**Set(PathMap<()>)**\nset algebra — lawful lattice\ntyped alias: `RholangSetPathMap`" as SetMode #C8E6C9
state "**Map(PathMap<Par>)**\nmap algebra — value slots\ntyped alias: `RholangMapPathMap`" as MapMode #E1BEE7

state "**AmbiguousEmpty**\nthe refusal, not a state of the value" as Ambiguous #FFE082

[*] --> Empty : `{| |}`

Empty -[#2E7D32,bold]-> SetMode : first **set** membership\noperation selects the mode
Empty -[#6A1B9A,bold]-> MapMode : first **map** operation\n(e.g. `set(k, v)`)\nselects the mode

Empty -[#EF6C00,dashed]right-> Ambiguous : mode-dependent mutation\n(e.g. `setSubtrie`)\non neutral empty
Ambiguous -[#EF6C00,dashed]-> Empty : caller must select\na mode first; the\nvalue is unchanged

SetMode -[#C62828,dashed]-> SetMode : **map** membership op → **rejected**\n(mixed set/map membership is unspellable)
SetMode -[#2E7D32]-> SetMode : set ops over the `PathMap<()>` lattice:\njoin · meet · subtract · restrict · zipper walks

MapMode -[#C62828,dashed]-> MapMode : **set** membership op\n→ **rejected**
MapMode -[#6A1B9A]-> MapMode : map ops over `PathMap<Par>`: `get` · `set` ·\n`delete` · join/meet with `ValueConflict` on\nunequal overlap · key-mask subtraction

SetMode -[hidden]down-> MapMode
Ambiguous -[hidden]down-> MapMode

note as NSET #E8F5E9
  ★ **An empty selected trie stays selected** when it
  carries explicit value-free terminating topology:
  `PathMap::is_empty` distinguishes *"no terminating path"*
  from *"no associated value"*.  Value-free topology
  therefore survives Eq / Hash / Ord and every wire
  round trip.
end note

note as NAMB #FFF3E0
  ★ **Why refuse rather than guess.** An entirely
  neutral `{| |}` cannot answer a mode-dependent
  mutation without silently choosing an algebra.
  `AmbiguousEmpty` is the edge case that prevents
  empty from selecting the wrong lattice on the
  caller's behalf.
end note

MapMode -[hidden]down-> NSET
MapMode -[hidden]down-> NAMB

legend bottom
  |= cell |= meaning |
  |<#ECEFF1>| mode-neutral empty |
  |<#C8E6C9>| set mode — `PathMap<()>`, lawful lattice |
  |<#E1BEE7>| map mode — `PathMap<Par>`, value-bearing |
  |<#FFE082>| `AmbiguousEmpty` refusal on neutral empty |
  |<#FFCDD2>| mixed set/map membership rejection |
endlegend

@enduml
